# List interruption

Setting: `ext_list_interrupts`. On in the Markdown-like profile.

In djot a list needs a blank line before it. With this setting a list
marker on the line after paragraph text starts a list.

``` example
Things to do:
- one
- two
.
<p>Things to do:</p>
<ul>
<li>
one
</li>
<li>
two
</li>
</ul>
```

This also lets a sublist follow an item's text directly.

``` example
- fruit
  - apple
  - pear
.
<ul>
<li>
fruit
<ul>
<li>
apple
</li>
<li>
pear
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
```

An ordered marker starts a list only when its number is `1`. Other numbers
often end a sentence.

``` example
The civil war ended in
1865. And this should not start a list.
.
<p>The civil war ended in
1865. And this should not start a list.</p>
```

``` example
The steps are
1. first
2. second
.
<p>The steps are</p>
<ol>
<li>
first
</li>
<li>
second
</li>
</ol>
```

## What it costs

A paragraph can no longer be wrapped anywhere: a line that begins with a
bullet or with `1.` starts a list.

